{# Values read from the pricing plan (DB, editable in the Console; falls back to constants). #}
{% set plan = plan_tarifaire() %}
{% set readWeight = plan.readWeight %}
{% set freeAllowance = plan.freeAllowance|format_nombre(0, 'en') %}
{% set freeWindowHours = plan.freeWindowHours %}
{% set docBase = plan.documentBase %}
{% set docParPage = plan.documentParPage %}
{% set docCarPage = plan.documentCaracteresParPage %}
{% set franchiseLignes = plan.echangeFranchiseLignes|format_nombre(0, 'en') %}

<p class="cgu-intro">
    On Joseara, the <strong>token</strong> is the unit measuring your usage of the platform.
    It enables fair, pay-as-you-go pricing while keeping a renewable <strong>free tier</strong>
    to get started and work day to day.
</p>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>1. What is a token?</h2>
    <p>
        A token measures the volume of data exchanged between your browser and our servers.
        Each operation "weighs" a number of tokens, deducted from your balance.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>2. When are tokens consumed?</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Output (reading)</strong>: every entity displayed/downloaded to your screen costs <strong>{{ readWeight }} tokens</strong>. Loading a list of 20 items therefore costs 20 × {{ readWeight }} = {{ 20 * readWeight }} tokens.</li>
        <li><strong>Input (writing)</strong>: every save (creation or update) costs a variable weight depending on the entity type.</li>
        <li><strong>AI assistant (premium)</strong>: every message sent to the assistant is metered as a write (see the "AI assistant message" weight below). The assistant is <strong>reserved for accounts with a paid token balance</strong> — the free allowance is not enough.</li>
            <li><strong>Documents produced by the assistant (premium)</strong>: when the assistant writes a downloadable document (Word, Excel, PDF…), its production is charged based on length and format — see §4. The exact cost is always shown <strong>before</strong> you approve the production.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>3. Entity weights on write</h2>
    <table class="cgu-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Entity</th><th>Weight (tokens)</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for fqcn, poids in plan.writeWeights %}
            <tr>
                <td>
                    <span class="cgu-entity">
                        <span class="cgu-entity-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ ux_icon(resolve_icon_name(token_entite_icon(fqcn)), {height:'18px', width:'18px'}) }}</span>
                        <span>{{ token_entite_label(fqcn, 'en') }}</span>
                    </span>
                </td>
                <td>{{ poids }}</td>
            </tr>
            {% endfor %}
            <tr>
                <td>
                    <span class="cgu-entity">
                        <span class="cgu-entity-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ ux_icon(resolve_icon_name('default'), {height:'18px', width:'18px'}) }}</span>
                        <span>Any other entity</span>
                    </span>
                </td>
                <td>{{ plan.defaultWriteWeight }}</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>
                    <span class="cgu-entity">
                        <span class="cgu-entity-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ ux_icon(resolve_icon_name('action:view'), {height:'18px', width:'18px'}) }}</span>
                        <span>Read (per entity, output)</span>
                    </span>
                </td>
                <td>{{ readWeight }}</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>4. Documents produced by the assistant</h2>
    <p>
        The assistant can <strong>build a downloadable document</strong> (Word, Excel, PDF, Markdown,
        plain text, web page) from an analysis: a structured report, meant to be used outside the
        platform. The cost follows this formula:
    </p>
    <p class="cgu-formule">
        <strong>({{ docBase }} + number of pages × {{ docParPage }}) × format coefficient</strong>,
        where a page is {{ docCarPage|format_nombre(0, 'en') }} characters (rounded up, minimum one page).
    </p>
    <table class="cgu-table">
        <thead>
            <tr><th>Format</th><th>Coefficient</th><th>Example: 3 pages</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        {% for format, coefficient in plan.documentFormats %}
            <tr class="cgu-format-row">
                <td>
                    <span class="cgu-entity">
                        <span class="cgu-entity-icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ ux_icon(resolve_icon_name('document'), {height:'18px', width:'18px'}) }}</span>
                        <span>{{ token_format_document_label(format, 'en') }}</span>
                    </span>
                </td>
                <td>×{{ coefficient|format_nombre(2, 'en')|replace({'.00': ''}) }}</td>
                <td><strong>{{ token_cout_document(3, format)|format_nombre(0, 'en') }}</strong> tokens</td>
            </tr>
        {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="cgu-note">
        The exact cost is <strong>always shown before</strong> you approve the production, and
        <strong>nothing is charged if you cancel</strong>.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>5. The free tier (Basic)</h2>
    <p>
        Every account receives <strong>{{ freeAllowance }} free tokens</strong>, automatically
        <strong>renewed every {{ freeWindowHours }} hours</strong>. The counter starts on your first activity after
        account creation. Free tokens do not accumulate: at each renewal, the free balance is
        reset to {{ freeAllowance }}.
    </p>
    <p>
        To get started friction-free, <strong>creating your very first company is free</strong>:
        no tokens are charged during the welcome assistant. Additional companies are then billed
        at the usual weight (see the table above).
    </p>
</section>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>6. Prepaid packs</h2>
    <p>Need more? You can buy <strong>stackable</strong> packs:</p>
    <table class="cgu-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Pack</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            {% for key, p in plan.packs %}
            <tr><td>{{ p.label|default(key|capitalize) }} — {{ p.tokens|format_nombre(0, 'en') }} tokens</td><td>{{ p.price|format_montant(0, 'en') }}</td></tr>
            {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
        Prepaid tokens are consumed first; once depleted, you automatically fall back to the
        free tier ({{ freeAllowance }} tokens / {{ freeWindowHours }} h).
    </p>
</section>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>7. What happens when tokens run out?</h2>
    <p>
        When your balance (free + prepaid) is no longer enough, <strong>reading and writing are
        temporarily blocked</strong>. You can then either <strong>top up</strong> a pack or
        <strong>wait for the next renewal</strong> of your free allowance (within {{ freeWindowHours }} hours).
    </p>
</section>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>8. Importing and exporting your data</h2>
    <p>
        <strong>Exporting is free and unlimited.</strong> What you take out of Joseara costs you
        nothing, and never will: your data is yours, and being able to take it back at any time is
        part of what you are buying.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Migrating your history</strong> &mdash; uploading a filled-in template &mdash; is
        included up to <strong>{{ franchiseLignes }} rows</strong> of the <em>DONNEES</em> sheet, for
        the lifetime of each firm. What counts is <strong>rows</strong>, not the records they
        produce: a single row that creates a client, a risk, an insurer, a policy and its instalment
        still uses <strong>one</strong> row.
    </p>
    <p>
        Beyond that, migration carries no flat fee: each row simply pays the
        <strong>ordinary write metering</strong> of the records it creates &mdash; exactly what the
        same data entry would have cost on screen, no more. The total is
        <strong>shown to you before you confirm</strong>, converted into dollars, and the migration
        will not start if your balance does not cover it.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="cgu-section">
    <h2>9. Who pays and who consumes?</h2>
    <p>
        The <strong>company owner</strong> pays. Any activity performed within a company — by its
        owner <em>or</em> by invited collaborators — is deducted from that company owner's balance.
    </p>
</section>
